<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Monday, barrows and gilts were $1.00 higher. Top $55.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>Snows and adverse weather conditions across hog country reduced marketings. Interior Iowa moved only 88,000 Monday.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs    54.50-55.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs    53.00-54.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady. Top $54.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-450 lbs    45.00</p>
<p>		  450-500 lbs    47.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3    500-550 lbs    51.00</p>
<p>		  550-700 lbs    53.00-54.00</p>
<p>    Boars - 300-700 lbs    41.00</p>
<p>		200-300 lbs    42.00</p>
</text>
